$COMMENT Generic Commercial Airplane Rotor Burst Model
$COMMENT
$COMMENT William Pease - 418400D
$COMMENT 24 February 2012
$COMMENT
$COMMENT Earlier version:
$COMMENT LeAnne McKay
$COMMENT 31 Aug 2000
$COMMENT
$COMMENT The generic aircraft models were developed in support of the Federal
$COMMENT Aviation Administration's Aircraft Catastrophic Failure Prevention
$COMMENT Program. The models are used to demonstrate the Uncontained Engine
$COMMENT Debris Damage Assessment Model (UEDDAM) tool which evaluates the risk
$COMMENT to the aircraft from uncontained engine failures.  This analysis
$COMMENT supports certification to Title 14 Code of Federal Regulations,
$COMMENT Part 25.903.  The models are for demonstration purposes and do not
$COMMENT depict actual aircraft and /or Aircraft systems in service.  The models
$COMMENT are available for public release.
$COMMENT
$COMMENT Note:  Right and left are with respect to looking forward
$COMMENT        from the tail; i.e. the pilot's perspective
$COMMENT ---------------------------------------------------------
$COMMENT    4004 is fuel in center tank but for 30% is empty - 
$COMMENT         4004 & 4005 are both assigned to ullage for 30%
$COMMENT    4007 and 4009 are COMPSPLTS for wing tanks 180.66 at 30%
COMPSPLT       4       4       4       5  170.50
COMPSPLT       4       2       4       7  180.66
COMPSPLT       4       3       4       9  180.66
$COMMENT
